    "result_text": "Done. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`. I followed the existing pattern used for other derived read-only owner fields (`membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`), which are `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` entity mapped by name into the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` returning `Integer`, computing the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (non-digits skipped, rightmost digit doubled first, `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`) \u2014 exactly matching the reference `luhn(...)` the test uses. Null/empty `customerCode` yields `0`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct auto-maps it from `getCheckDigit()` by name (no explicit mapper `@Mapping` needed, same as `membershipLevel`/`contactPreference`).\n\nResult: `POST /api/owners` then `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `checkDigit` equal to the Luhn digit of the returned `customerCode`. Test suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
